meta {
  name: Consent
  seq: 13
}

docs {
  # Consent scenarios

  BDD scenarios for the consent lifecycle. An enterprise asks a person for consent, the
  person answers in the Altinn portal, and the enterprise (or Maskinporten on its behalf)
  reads the result.

  | Step | Endpoint | Caller | Token |
  |---|---|---|---|
  | Create request | POST /accessmanagement/api/v1/enterprise/consentrequests | enterprise | Maskinporten, altinn:consentrequests.write |
  | Read request | GET /accessmanagement/api/v1/enterprise/consentrequests/:id | enterprise | Maskinporten, altinn:consentrequests.read or .write |
  | Status events | GET /accessmanagement/api/v1/enterprise/consentrequests/events | enterprise | Maskinporten, altinn:consentrequests.read or .write |
  | Read request | GET /accessmanagement/api/v1/bff/consentrequests/:requestId | portal user | personal, altinn:portal/enduser |
  | Count pending | GET /accessmanagement/api/v1/bff/consentrequests/count/:partyUuid | portal user | personal, altinn:portal/enduser |
  | List requests | GET /accessmanagement/api/v1/bff/consentrequests/list/:partyUuid | portal user | personal, altinn:portal/enduser |
  | Accept | POST /accessmanagement/api/v1/bff/consentrequests/:requestId/accept | portal user | personal, altinn:portal/enduser |
  | Reject | POST /accessmanagement/api/v1/bff/consentrequests/:requestId/reject | portal user | personal, altinn:portal/enduser |
  | Read consent | GET /accessmanagement/api/v1/bff/consents/:consentId/ | portal user | personal, altinn:portal/enduser |
  | Revoke | POST /accessmanagement/api/v1/bff/consents/:consentId/revoke | portal user | personal, altinn:portal/enduser |
  | Lookup | POST /accessmanagement/api/v1/maskinporten/consent/lookup | Maskinporten | altinn:maskinporten/consent.read |

  A consent request and the consent it becomes share one id. The enterprise API speaks
  external identifiers (urn:altinn:person:identifier-no, urn:altinn:organization:identifier-no);
  the BFF answers with internal party uuids (urn:altinn:party:uuid).

  Each subfolder is one scenario. The files inside are the scenario steps, named
  `NN_GIVEN|WHEN|THEN|AND|CLEANUP_...` and ordered by `seq`.

  ## State and cleanup

  Consent requests cannot be deleted. Every scenario creates fresh requests with a new id
  and never relies on the absence of earlier ones; counts and lists are asserted relative
  to a baseline or by id. Each request a scenario creates ends in a final state (revoked or
  rejected), so no run leaves a pending request in the person's portal inbox.

  ## Personas and fixtures

  Seed data comes from `testdata/consent/<env>.js`, tokens from `helpers.js`:

  - Enterprise: the organization asking for consent (Maskinporten token, consumer claim).
  - Other enterprise: an unrelated organization, for the read negatives.
  - Consenting person: the person asked for consent, who acts in the portal.
  - Other person: a person with no rights for the consenting person.
  - Consent resource: `samtykke-performance-test`, which requires the metadata key
    `inntektsaar`.

  ## Environments

  Runs against AT22. Testdata exists for AT22 only; the persons and the consent resource
  have not been confirmed in other environments.

  ## Timing

  The events endpoint only returns events older than five minutes (the
  ConsentEventsSafetyLag setting), so events for requests created in the same run are not
  visible yet. The events steps assert shape and filtering on whatever older events exist.
}
